l},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Close the --status/--clean TOCTOU gap: assert the equality on the SAME foreign set --clean acts upon (e.g. capture --clean's own reported target set and re-assert byte-equality to the 8 ids, aborting if --clean would touch any un-triaged path), rather than asserting only on a prior --status snapshot.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T9","project.engine-layer-enforcement"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'immediately before the write, --status's foreign list must be exactly the 8 triaged ids'","'for name in foreign:' ... 'shutil.rmtree(full) on every entry that fsck.foreign_store_path_list returned'","'--clean' re-derives foreign set independently — the equality assertion is on --status output, not on --clean's own scan","'bounds the check-then-act (TOCTOU) window to the gap between that --status and the --clean, seconds apart'"],"finding":"The run-level equality gate asserts on `--status`'s foreign list, but `--clean` re-derives its own foreign set from a fresh `fsck` scan at clean-time; the plan does not guarantee the acted-on set equals the asserted set. A 9th empty stray dir created in the seconds-wide window between `--status` and `--clean` would be swept by the all-or-nothing `--clean` without ever appearing in the attested 8 ids.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7275b98ac1609411","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Section 'How --clean actually behaves' and AC2/AC3","norm_id":"n7f8c09d01cee416a","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A concurrent interrupted write creates a 9th empty dir after the --status equality check passes but before --clean runs; --clean's fresh fsck lists 9, rmtree deletes all 9, and the audit/attestation names only 8 — an unattested deletion."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Clarify that `--clean` recomputes the foreign set internally so the AC2 equality assertion is advisory (not an enforced delete-set filter), and state that safety against a mid-window 9th stray rests on the classifier only ever deleting event-less directories.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'immediately before the write, --status's foreign list must be exactly the 8 triaged ids. If it lists any 9th path ... the run is ABORTED'","Code: tracker_maintenance.py L200 `foreign = _foreign_worktree_paths(tracker)` then L242 `for name in foreign:` recomputes and deletes with no gate against the operator's asserted list","ABSENCE: no mechanism in --clean consumes or compares against the AC2-asserted 8-id list"],"finding":"The AC2 equality gate is enforced by the operator's out-of-band `--status`, but `rebar tracker-maintenance --clean` independently RE-computes the foreign set inside the process (tracker_maintenance.py L200, L242) and deletes whatever it computes; the operator's byte-equality assertion does not constrain what the tool actually removes. If a 9th event-less stray appears in the TOCTOU window between AC2's `--status` and AC3's `--clean`, `--clean` will delete it too despite AC2 having asserted exactly-8. The plan frames the gate as if it selects the delete set ('applied as an equality check ... the run is ABORTED'), but the tool has no such gate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3959d307229d3d66","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Section 'How --clean actually behaves' and AC2/AC3","norm_id":"na282007ff0759b7d","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A concurrent interrupted write creates a 9th empty stray in the seconds between the pre-write --status and --clean; --clean deletes all 9, not the asserted 8"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Restate AC2/AC3 to compare the SET of `? `-prefixed entries parsed from `--status` (stripping the `  ? ` prefix and ignoring the count header) against the 8 triaged ids, rather than a raw byte-equal comparison of the whole `foreign top-level paths` block.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.735,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'its `foreign top-level paths` list is asserted byte-equal to the 8 triaged ids'","tracker_maintenance.py:158-160: `sys.stdout.write(f\"foreign top-level paths : {len(foreign)}\\n\")` then `for p in foreign: sys.stdout.write(f\"  ? {p}\\n\")` — output is prefixed/indented, not a bare id list","MATCH on subcommand/flag existence; the mismatch is in the ASSERTED output shape the equality gate depends on"],"finding":"AC2 asserts the `--status` `foreign top-level paths` output is 'byte-equal to the 8 triaged ids', but the verified `_report` render emits a `foreign top-level paths : <n>` count header followed by indented `  ? <name>` lines (tracker_maintenance.py:158-160), never a bare newline-joined list of 8 ids — so a literal byte-equal check can never pass and the equality gate is not implementable as written.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3fd9cafa9ab00594","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC2 / AC3","norm_id":"n3a3d79040ad04852","priority":0.165,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["Operator scripts a byte-equal comparison of raw --status stdout against the 8 ids and it fails despite the set being correct, or worse writes a comparison that silently never matches"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Specify: extract the names from lines matching `^  \\? (\\S+)$` in --status stdout and assert that set equals the 8 triaged ids (and that the count header reads 8); drop 'byte-equal'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"